# Replica skills (installed)

This project has the Replica suite at `.claude/skills/replica-*/` (11 skills, MIT,
from github.com/Jakeschincariol/replica-skill).

To run one, open its `SKILL.md` and follow it as a mode:
`.claude/skills/replica-recon/SKILL.md`, `replica-architect`, `replica-design`,
`replica-build`, `replica-backend`, `replica-test`, `replica-diff`,
`replica-entrepreneur`, `replica-brand`, `replica-launch`, `replica-deploy`.

Python helpers are stdlib-only, no pip install, e.g.:

```
python3 .claude/skills/replica-design/contrast.py replica/design/tokens.json
python3 .claude/skills/replica-diff/parity.py <args>
```

## Rules that apply to every replica workflow

- **Clean-room only.** Rebuild features and user flows. Never copy another
  product's code, logo, copy, content, or assets.
- **Never type passwords, card numbers, or live API keys** into any page or file.
  The user creates third-party accounts (Stripe, Supabase, Resend, Google Cloud)
  and puts keys in `.env.local`. Generate `.env.example` with names and no values.
- Keep skills' outputs inside this repo under `replica/`.
